From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:10:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: publish the caching state when it changes

The published caching flag followed the player's state only at the
next play state update. A player thread blocked right after leaving
caching, such as on a decoder close at a clip join, kept the skin's
buffering indicator up for that whole time.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
       m_playSpeed = speed;
 
       m_caching = CACHESTATE_DONE;
+      {
+        std::unique_lock lock(m_StateSection);
+        m_State.caching = false;
+      }
       m_clock.SetSpeed(speed);
       m_VideoPlayerAudio->SetSpeed(speed);
       m_VideoPlayerVideo->SetSpeed(speed);
@@ -0,6 +0,9 @@
   m_caching = state;
 
   m_clock.SetSpeedAdjust(0);
+
+  std::unique_lock lock(m_StateSection);
+  m_State.caching = m_caching > CACHESTATE_DONE && m_caching < CACHESTATE_PLAY;
 }
 
 void CVideoPlayer::SetPlaySpeed(int speed)
